    "result_text": "The build is green. There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and the full suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date, returning **400 Bad Request**.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`FutureRegistrationDateException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` following the existing exception convention in the `rest.advice` package.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after reading the supplied `registrationDate`, if it is present and `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`, throw `FutureRegistrationDateException`. The check runs on the *raw supplied* date, before defaulting-to-today or the business-day roll-forward, so a future date is rejected rather than silently normalized.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added `@ExceptionHandler(FutureRegistrationDateException.class)` mapping it to a 400 `ProblemDetail` with an `errors` array naming the `registrationDate` field, matching how the sibling validation errors (telephone, email, postcode) are reported.\n\nThe `errorRejectsFutureDate` acceptance test (posting `registrationDate: \"2999-01-01\"`) now returns 400, and all existing tests remain green.",
